@EndUserText.label: 'Granting access control to draft table'
@MappingRole: true


//By default, when you only specify draft table <draft_table>, the RAP runtime reads active instances through your CDS Entity (which supports DCL access control), but reads draft instances directly from the draft database table (<draft_table>).
//
//Because ABAP Dictionary database tables cannot have CDS Access Controls (DCL) attached directly to them, reading directly from the draft table bypasses DCL checks unless you place a CDS view (Draft Query View) in front of it.
//
//(Note: RAP still performs all transactional `INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE` draft writes directly against `<draft_table>`; the `<draft_query_view>` is usedonly for read/query operations.)
//
//
//When Do You Use query <draft_query_view>?
//
//    1. Enforcing CDS Access Control (DCL) on Drafts (Primary Use Case)
//    2. In Fiori Elements apps (e.g., List Reports with Editing Status = All or Own Draft / Unsaved Changes by Another User), users can query draft records.
//    3. Without a draft query view + DCL, users who have access to the app could see draft records belonging to organizational units (e.g., Sales Organizations, Company Codes) 
//       they are not authorized for, or see other users' private drafts.
//    4. Defining a <draft_query_view> lets you attach a DCL (DEFINE ROLE) to enforce pfcg_auth checks or user-based restrictions (e.g., = aspect user on CreatedByUser) on 
//       draft data.
//    5. Security & ATC Checks in Production RAP BOs
//    6. If your active CDS entity is protected by a DCL, standard security guidelines (and ATC checks) expect draft instances to be similarly protected so sensitive 
//       data isn't exposed while in draft state.
//    7. SQL-Level Calculated / Derived Fields During Draft Reads
//    8. While draft tables persist the columns of the entity, if your active CDS view computes certain read-only/display fields dynamically via SQL expressions or 
//       associations (and you don't want to maintain them via RAP determination logic in the draft table), the draft query view can compute those expressions dynamically on read.

define role ZMRG_DRAFT_TABLE_ACCES_CONTROL {
    grant 
        select
            on
                ZMRG_DRAFT_TABLE_ACCES_CONTROL
                    where
                       Employeeid is not initial;
                        
}